body: "Affected draft: [unbraind/pm-rust#92](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/92), head `ebc2deb36720bcd421126e55e88e4b0f50c098ed`.\n\n## Goal and scope\n\nThe [native orientation contract](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/ebc2deb36720bcd421126e55e88e4b0f50c098ed/docs/NATIVE_ORIENTATION.md#L67-L81) explicitly supports dependency trees, graphs, summary counts and visible missing references. The [canonical feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/ebc2deb36720bcd421126e55e88e4b0f50c098ed/.agents/pm/features/pm-rust-xb3s.toon) targets parity with the pinned published oracle. Missing parents are not among the [deferred controls](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/ebc2deb36720bcd421126e55e88e4b0f50c098ed/.agents/pm/tasks/pm-rust-s6j4.toon).\n\n## Reproduction\n\nIn a disposable initialized tracker, retain a valid Task named `sample-child` with `parent: sample-deleted`, no structured dependencies and no `blocked_by`, while `sample-deleted` is absent. This can arise after a parent is deleted while the child remains.\n\nRun each command against the same fixture with the native binary and the locked `@unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.14` oracle:\n\n- `deps sample-child --summary --json`\n- `deps sample-child --json`\n- `deps sample-child --format graph --json`\n\nExpected: the missing parent is exposed as an outgoing `parent` edge to `sample-deleted`. With default bounds, summary reports `node_count: 2`, `edge_count: 1`, `missing_count: 1`; tree and graph contain the missing target.\n\nNative result implied by the exact source: no edges, only the root, `node_count: 1`, `edge_count: 0`, `missing_count: 0`. The successful response hides a broken hierarchy reference from dependency-based diagnostics.\n\n## Cause and admitted-input proof\n\n[Native index construction](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/ebc2deb36720bcd421126e55e88e4b0f50c098ed/src/orientation_deps.rs#L43-L89) retains structured dependencies and synthesizes only dangling `blocked_by`; it never reads `metadata.parent`. All three projections use this index. [Summary counts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/ebc2deb36720bcd421126e55e88e4b0f50c098ed/src/orientation_deps.rs#L93-L115) follow only its dependency edges, and [the public summary path](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/ebc2deb36720bcd421126e55e88e4b0f50c098ed/src/orientation_deps.rs#L370-L384) returns those counts directly.\n\nThis input does not hit a native refusal: [ItemMetadata.parent](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/ebc2deb36720bcd421126e55e88e4b0f50c098ed/src/item.rs#L35-L40) accepts an optional string, [decode_item](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/ebc2deb36720bcd421126e55e88e4b0f50c098ed/src/item.rs#L90-L128) validates required fields and priority without checking parent existence, and [read_items_impl](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/ebc2deb36720bcd421126e55e88e4b0f50c098ed/src/workspace.rs#L177-L208) adds only duplicate-ID validation. The context-only derived-snapshot refusal is not called by deps.\n\nThe pinned oracle's [dangling collector](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/sdk/graph/assembly.ts#L336-L410) includes scalar `parent` references. [runDeps](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/sdk/dependencies.ts#L1257-L1280) merges them into the traversal index before tree, graph or summary projection.\n\n## Validation and regression criteria\n\nAn isolated, dependency-free Node control executed the unmodified pinned-oracle collector, index normalization, dangling merge block and graph counter. Six cases passed: missing parent on an open holder; missing parent on a terminal holder; an existing parent; an already-declared matching parent edge; missing `blocked_by`; and no reference. Missing-parent cases yielded the expected 2/1/1 counts. Existing-parent and no-reference controls yielded 1/0/0. Matching explicit edges were not duplicated.\n\nThe native side is established by the exact source path, not an executed native CLI: no Rust compiler or native binary was available in the review workspace. No dependencies were installed, no real tracker was changed, and no full native/oracle differential suite is claimed.\n\nBefore closing, add real-CLI differential cases for these controls in both JSON and TOON and for tree, graph and summary. Assert bounded behavior (particularly max-depth zero), mixed-case/trimmed parent IDs, and no duplicate edge when an equivalent structured parent reference already exists. The missing-parent case should fail against the current implementation and pass with the correction; keep read-only tracker-byte assertions.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (6)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T12:00:19Z)\n>\n> Fixed in PR #92, commit `ad0169babce474547c6e4ac559eec900a23ccf5c`. Dangling scalar parents now enter the normalized traversal index in oracle order, including terminal holders, without duplicating matching structured parent edges. Existing parents add no synthetic traversal edge. `cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential deps_dangling_parents_match_oracle` passes ten controls across tree/graph/summary, JSON/TOON and default/depth-zero bounds (120 real native/oracle comparisons), including trimmed/mixed-case identities, duplicate-edge controls and unchanged item/history bytes. Reverting only index construction fails on the missing-parent 1/0/0 versus oracle 2/1/1 receipt. The additional scalar-sentinel regression also matches the pinned oracle. Clean `just release-check` passes 456 normal and 456 instrumented tests with all four coverage dimensions at 100%; strict health passes in a fresh no-local clone. The PR body includes `Fixes #93`. Leaving the issue open for orchestrator verification and merge.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T13:04:02Z)\n>\n> The real missing-parent case is now addressed, and the final-head CI logs are green, but the fix introduces a smaller parent-normalization mismatch that should be covered before closing this issue.\n> \n> ## Residual static finding: ignored parent placeholders become missing nodes\n> \n> Reviewed PR #92 at `c511d607579d746e201a15e54a37b287c79b1195`. This remains within the [claimed tree/graph/summary oracle-parity scope](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/c511d607579d746e201a15e54a37b287c79b1195/docs/NATIVE_ORIENTATION.md#L83-L97) and [canonical orientation feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/c511d607579d746e201a15e54a37b287c79b1195/.agents/pm/features/pm-rust-xb3s.toon).\n> \n> In a disposable initialized tracker, use a valid stored Task `sample-child` with the scalar string `parent: none`, no structured dependencies and no blocker. The same discrepancy applies to string `null` (quote it in TOON), `n/a`, `na`, and mixed-case/whitespace variants.\n> \n> For `deps sample-child --summary --json` with default depth:\n> - Pinned oracle: `node_count: 1, edge_count: 0, missing_count: 0`\n> - Current native source implies: `node_count: 2, edge_count: 1, missing_count: 1`, with a synthesized `parent` edge to the placeholder\n> \n> Tree and graph share the same index, so they also acquire a nonexistent target. Imported or legacy documents using these empty-reference markers would produce false missing-parent diagnostics.\n> \n> ## Exact source evidence and admitted input\n> \n> The new [scalar-reference loop](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/c511d607579d746e201a15e54a37b287c79b1195/src/orientation_deps.rs#L76-L100) skips only empty strings, known IDs and duplicate edges. It does not apply the oracle's [reference normalizer](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/sdk/graph/assembly.ts#L74-L86), which explicitly drops `none`, `null`, `n/a` and `na` after trimming and lowercasing. That normalizer is called by the [actual dangling collector](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/sdk/graph/assembly.ts#L349-L380), whose results [feed deps traversal](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/sdk/dependencies.ts#L1249-L1280).\n> \n> These are admitted stored strings: native [ItemMetadata/decoding](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/c511d607579d746e201a15e54a37b287c79b1195/src/item.rs#L35-L38) accepts an optional string, and its [validation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/c511d607579d746e201a15e54a37b287c79b1195/src/item.rs#L90-L128) does not reject these parent values. Oracle metadata reads likewise retain nonempty parent strings through [trimStringOrUndefined](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/core/item/item-format.ts#L1312-L1316) and [parent normalization](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/core/item/item-format.ts#L1742); reference filtering happens afterward. This is a stored-document/read-path finding, not a claim that current create/update commands accept every placeholder.\n> \n> ## Validation and limits\n> \n> An isolated dependency-free Node run executed the exact pinned-oracle collector, dependency normalization, dangling merge block, graph counter and string-normalizer extracts: 44 case/depth controls passed. These include the original missing-parent cases, eight placeholder spellings, existing/duplicate references, `no-active-blocker`, explicit structured references and depth zero.\n> \n> Two narrowly changed oracle-extract controls failed as intended: removing only placeholder filtering produced 2/1/1 instead of 1/0/0; suppressing only scalar-parent insertion produced the original 1/0/0 instead of 2/1/1 defect. These are executed helper controls, not native-binary or complete-CLI runs. No Rust toolchain/native executable was available locally.\n> \n> Please add real native/oracle comparisons for these stored parent placeholders across tree/graph/summary, JSON/TOON and default/depth-zero bounds, retaining read-only byte checks. Preserve the oracle's distinct behavior for `no-active-blocker` and explicit structured dependencies; a broad “drop all sentinel-looking edges” change would be incorrect.\n> \n> All 93 all-state GitHub issue/PR records and all 72 exact-head canonical PM items were checked for ownership. This is additional evidence for the same scalar-parent parity issue, so no duplicate issue is needed.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T13:41:12Z)\n>\n> Current-head validation after the second review is green at `180bb80e44c3eb4cb433330d76955c481df7287f`. `cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential deps_dangling_parents_match_oracle` retains all ten controls across tree/graph/summary, JSON/TOON and default/depth-zero bounds (120 real comparisons); the sentinel regression adds 12. Both clean release-gate passes include them. The new one-time corpus identity set preserves the corrected dangling-parent behavior. The existing single-fix dangling-parent revert proof remains recorded in PM; Fixes #93 remains in the PR body. Leaving the issue open for orchestrator verification.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T14:51:48Z)\n>\n> Test-only review head `25ef9ecb57a110f2a3ffc41e63007bbae88e61aa` preserves the issue #93 correction. Both complete release-gate passes include `cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential deps_dangling_parents_match_oracle` (120 real projection/encoding/bounds comparisons) and the sentinel regression. Production source is byte-identical to 180bb80; the only test change strengthens closed-pipe acceptance. Fixes #93 remains in the PR body; leaving this issue open for orchestrator verification.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T16:51:58Z)\n>\n> Latest review head ef276adb0316de850d89605ea295e9e997bf4ac8 retains the dangling-parent correction and its 120 real-CLI controls in cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential deps_dangling_parents_match_oracle. The full orientation suite passes 18 tests, and the isolated release gate passes 464 normal + 464 instrumented tests with all four coverage dimensions at 100%. Fixes #93 remains in the PR body. The issue stays open for orchestrator verification; all-OS CI is running on this head.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T18:57:55Z)\n>\n> Issue #93 closed at the PR #92 merge, but the scalar-placeholder residual in [the earlier review](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/issues/93#issuecomment-6250251689) is still present in merged main.\n> \n> The final reviewed PR head `ef276adb0316de850d89605ea295e9e997bf4ac8` and merge `368697864187e347ed17c5a1e7dfc00284cf4e26` have the identical Git tree `cba4fb13676ed624a84037d4940fc10d648e6258`. The [merged scalar-reference loop](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/368697864187e347ed17c5a1e7dfc00284cf4e26/src/orientation_deps.rs#L80-L105) still skips only empty, existing and duplicate references, so a stored `parent: none` (also string `null`, `n/a`, `na`, including case/whitespace variants) implies native summary 2 nodes / 1 edge / 1 missing; the pinned oracle ignores that scalar reference and reports 1 / 0 / 0. The [existing sentinel regression](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/368697864187e347ed17c5a1e7dfc00284cf4e26/tests/orientation_differential.rs#L137-L178) covers `blocked_by: no-active-blocker`, which intentionally has different behavior; it does not cover these parent placeholders.\n> \n> I reran the dependency-free exact pinned-oracle helper controls: 44 case/depth controls pass; removing only placeholder filtering fails as expected, as does removing only scalar-parent insertion. The native result remains a static source finding because this review workspace has no Rust toolchain or native executable. Merged-main all-platform CI is green, but those tests do not cover this residual.\n> \n> Please reopen or otherwise retain ownership of this residual in the existing issue, add real native/oracle comparisons for stored parent placeholders across tree/graph/summary, JSON/TOON and default/depth-zero bounds, and preserve the distinct `no-active-blocker` and explicit structured-dependency behavior. The original genuine missing-parent correction is verified and should stay intact.\n>"
